<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Omnia year earnings, dividend jump.</title>
<headline>Omnia year earnings, dividend jump.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     158.2	 vs 98.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 62.0	  vs 52.0</p>
<p>    After-tax income	62.23	 vs 38.51</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   69.15	 vs 40.93</p>
<p>    Tax			 8.68	  vs 3.49</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,062.99    vs 834.21</p>
<p>Div payable May 9</p>
<p>on register April 11</p>
<p>Full name: Omnia Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Attributable to outside shareholders 0.89  vs 0.26</p>
<p>NOTE - Fertiliser to industrial chemicals firm Omnia said that prospects for the fertiliser industry were promising.</p>
<p>The firm added that its mining explosives, industrial chemicals and international operations are expected to further improve net income, aided by a full year contribution from plants commissioned in 1996.</p>
<p>The firm said it expected to produce a real improvement in earnings in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
